  "hostNotes": "Accept any animal found wild or feral in Australia with a credible fatal mechanism (venom, bite, kick, disease vector, or toxic if eaten); decide before play whether non-native animals (horse, cattle, dog, camel, deer, cane toad, bee) count, and apply it consistently. Generic answers (snake, shark, spider, jellyfish) are their own buckets by default; croc, octopus, funnel-web, taipan, brown snake and stinger auto-map to the obvious species. Likely traps: white-tailed spider, huntsman, daddy long legs, scorpion, centipede, koala, drop bear and Gympie-Gympie (a plant) should be rejected; platypus, emu, goanna, scrub python and crown-of-thorns starfish are venomous or dangerous but have no confirmed human deaths, so treat them as host-discretion half-credit at best."
}
